# Tool input validation

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Issue | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
| Status | Draft |

The registry enforces the JSON Schema supplied to providers before invoking a tool executor, allowing the model to correct malformed calls within the existing tool-round budget.

## Contract

- Invalid required fields, declared types and enum values produce a readable ToolResponse naming the property path and constraint, never an input value, without invoking the executor; logs likewise contain no input values, valid inputs including unknown keys pass through unchanged without coercion or defaults exactly once, and only an unknown tool name throws.
- Static schemas compile during registration, an uncompilable schema throws an error naming the tool at that point, and execution reuses the compiled schema across calls.
- Function-valued definitions validate against the currently resolved schema each call, caching compilation by resolved schema object rather than tool name.
